# The published seed knows none of the nineteen `__Builtins.debug*`/`__Builtins.*Machine` names this tree
# adds, so it refuses the tree at every call that spells one (E3004). All nineteen are called from this one
# function, which is what lets one patch withdraw the whole band: the parser arms, the runtime installer and
# the name constants are left standing, so `C1` knows them and compiles the unshimmed tree into `C2`.
#
# The shimmed funnel answers 0 to every verb. Zero is FALSE for each of the bool verbs and "the pin was
# refused" for the pin, so the first build's debugger refuses to start a session rather than reading wrong
# words out of a live process. It keeps ONE host call the seed does know, because `releaseDebugSessionPin`
# discards the funnel's answer and a pure function's discarded result is E3064. The call is the uptime clock
# rather than anything else the seed lowers: `HostFacility.uptimeClock` is `true` on all four native rows of
# the published seed's `TargetFacilities.targetProvidesFacility`, and `__uptime_ms` is a runtime-tier entry on
# no effect-free roster, so the discard is legal on every lane the first build runs on. A host call whose
# facility a lane withholds would make this shim a second E3104 in place of the E3004 it cures.
